A||||8||sully5||Finally did it.||||7||
Z||000000||sully5||03-28-2000||02:01 AM||||Well, it took me almost 3 hrs, but i finally finished changing the plugs in a Fiero for the first time. The first three I got done in less than 10 minutes. The others were a nightmare. I was able to get the socket in there but just could not get them to budge. As much as I didn't want to, I had to take the decklid off tonight. Even had to use a cheater bar. Called my dad to ask when the last time he changed them for my brother was, and he said never. My brother bought the car in 93! I love my brother to death but I still think the folks got the wrong kid from the hospital. One of the plugs was pitted so bad I am amazed that it came out at all, wihtout having to pull the head. I am tired and sore, so the wires will have to wait until tomorrow. Thanks for the space to let me vent. I feel better now.||||reg||7
Z||000001||GT Bastard||03-28-2000||02:58 AM||||Geez man!  It only took my 1/2 hour to do them all.  Then again, my arms are pretty long and skinny.  The plugs in the back looked pretty nasty!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phaeton||03-28-2000||03:30 AM||||I always thought the mechanics that told me the front plugs could be changed with the engine in the Fiero were just plain ignorant.  I have tried and failed more than once.  Lucky for me I wear out clutches faster than spark plugs and change them both out at the same time.<BR>But just the fact that it's possible bothers me, its terrible being the last to know when you're too old.||||reg||12
Z||000003||sully5||03-28-2000||08:51 AM||||GTB - I got skinny arms, too. Reaching the plugs wasn't the problem. It was the fact that they had been in for seven yrs. or more. Hopefully next time I'll be able to do it the 1/2 hr time frame.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||03-28-2000||09:25 AM||||I will, of course, be installing new plugs <B>before</B> I install the "new" engine! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||Standard||03-29-2000||08:43 PM||||Just replaced all the plugs in my car with some new NGK's.  Front  plugs were a piece of cake.  Took off the decklid right away for the firewall side.  Those weren't too bad, considering two of the three were only finger tight..  also got a chance to see where my manifold is cracked.. wow!  big crack on the top between cyl #4 and 6.  gotta replace that soon..||||reg||12
Z||000006||Gokart||03-29-2000||09:52 PM||||The 1st week I got my GT I changed the plugs and I'm saving the three I pulled from the back! Their kind of momentos of how someone could neglect such a beautiful car. They were so corroded rusted I could probably snap them in half with my hands!||||reg||2
Z||000007||Racer 1||03-30-2000||01:31 AM||||I get my plugs out in about 2 min for all for I have a air impact driver that helps out alot. But I only have 4 plugs.||||reg||10
Z||000008||DJRice||03-30-2000||11:42 AM||||Ive had my 87 for over 2 years now, and it has always run very strong and smooth.  However, last fall around Thanksgiving, I decided that it finally needed a tune up.  It was about a 3 hr job, and I found that the forward 3 plugs were the originals.  They were rusted in there pretty good and I really had to work them before I could get them out.<P>I am not a small guy, but once I had the decklid off, which I did before I even attempted to start to replace the front 3, I did not have much trouble getting to the plugs with a 1/4" drive rachet.  However, a small ratchet just wont break that kind of rust.||||reg||1
